  "body": "## Summary\n\nPR2743 leaves count tapes outside its complete first-node payload reserve. This adds a source-bound written count-storage proof for Jose Manuel/jmbarrancoml's unchanged PR2697 caller at `a53fdf4bcbe33c6732f0bec1badc8c023380f9d1`.\n\n```text\nparticipating cardinality tapes <= 98, rounded to 100\nsymbols per tape <= B + 2\ncount content <= 100 * (B + 2), excluding LEFT\nB = max(1, bit_length(V), indices.bits)\n```\n\nThe inventory includes borrowed arguments, Count.literal's simultaneous raw/returned tapes, product/add temporaries, marginal padding, countdowns, the original-offset peel and final merge. The fixed source callbacks and absent optional observer are explicit hypotheses. This is one reserve category; numerical/control/directory tapes, LEFT markers, physical placement, larger returns and total reserve admission remain open. There is no supplier or kappa change.\n\nOnly `research/selected-node-count-storage/` is added. It contains the proof, exact receipt, 43-routine inventory, bounded source archive, per-file source pins, standalone checker, 11 focused tests and registered replay hook. All 45 source exports independently match the pinned commit; predecessor notices and proof are unchanged. Credit Jose Manuel's caller, Nick Petalas's PR2708/2743 payload work, starship-s's PR2731 residual work, ywz65's directory/primitive work and retained lineage. PR2473's countdown time and PR2590's directory setup time are complementary scopes.\n\nTask card `selected-stock-envelope`, priority 5, is explicitly changed to the live [Discussion2319 handoff](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2319#discussioncomment-18957024). The original complex-track suggestions were checked before taking this current reserve component. Scoped source/lifetime and checker reviews found two issues that were fixed: arbitrary observers can mutate borrowed counts, and preloaded Python module names could bypass source imports.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before: complete caller payload evidence excludes count tapes, and a one-tape budget rejects Count.literal's real constructor overlap. After: the written source inventory gives 92 owned roots plus 6 borrowed counts, with transient padding explicitly priced.\n- The complete GL2 node at V=15,552 observes 119 occupied count symbols, at most 27 tapes and 15 symbols per tape across 119,351,262 count writes. All 5,712 child entries/returns complete; direct cell censuses, independent returned-bit checks, borrowed-input/head restoration and count cleanup pass. A separate literal n3/d2 peel at V=729 measures 66 symbols, 18 tapes and 11 symbols per tape.\n- Registered CPython 3.12.15 replay, optimized padding/peel controls and all 11 focused tests pass locally. The repository research-workflow suite passes 70 tests with 3 skips. Controls cover constructor underbudget, product/countdown behavior, inventory exhaustion, source/import/archive faults, recompression and typed receipts. Two internal reviewers checked the source proof and45 exact exports; no independent human, formal-kernel or hosted-CI pass is claimed.\n- Full selected GL64 payload execution, the selected supplier cold replay and total numerical stock admission are outside this component. The 100 cap is conservative rather than optimal. Successful execution is a premise; inherited exception cleanup is separate.\n\n```sh\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python -Werror -B scripts/research_package.py \\\n  --package research/selected-node-count-storage\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python -Werror -B -m unittest discover \\\n  -s tests -p 'test_research_*.py'\n```\n\nStarted from current canonical main `9ed84862fe4cb6eb67b2572eca332c92df803a1f`. Submission freshness and live-overlap coverage are recorded in TASK.json. Metadata coverage is not proof of novelty. Scientific source heads remain frozen.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way\n\nAdditive research package; production suppliers, selected result and predecessor packages are unchanged.\n\n**Blast Radius:** research\n",
